course: dictionary
lesson: 3011
title: Duvets and context clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A duvet is a big, soft bed cover. It is filled with feathers or other soft material, and you sleep under it to keep warm. Read this: «One night Mum finds her crying under the duvet.» You are under something, it is soft, and it is on a bed, so a duvet must be the bed cover.
explain: Other words around duvet give clues too. «Snuggle under the duvet» tells you it is cosy and warm. «Duvet cover» tells you the duvet has a cover on it, and that the cover is washed regularly. Look at the words next to an unknown word, not just the word itself.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. A duvet keeps you warm because it traps heat. The safety sentence shows this: «under a pillow or duvet the heat cannot escape». So the duvet keeps heat in, which is good for you in bed but dangerous for a phone.
fact: A duvet is a big, soft bed cover filled with feathers or other soft material.
fact: You sleep under a duvet to keep warm.
fact: A duvet cover is a removable cover that is washed regularly.
fact: A duvet day is a relaxing day at home, often spent in bed.
fact: Never cover a phone or charger with a duvet, because the heat cannot escape and it can start a fire.
exercise: «One night Mum finds her crying under the duvet.» What is a duvet? | *A big soft bed cover you sleep under to keep warm | A small bag for school books | A hard wooden table for eating
exercise: Why should you not put a charger under a duvet? | It makes the charger shiny | *Because the heat cannot escape, and it can start a fire | It makes the charger work faster
exercise: Copy the word that means a soft bed cover you sleep under, in: «Sam pulled the duvet up to his chin.» | lamp | door | *duvet | pillow
test: Why do you sleep under a duvet? | To hide from the teacher | *To keep warm | To cool down in summer | To keep dry in the rain
test: Which material can fill a duvet? | Metal and glass | Wood and stone | Sand and water | *Feathers or other soft material
exam: Read: «Electricity also makes heat: chargers buried in a duvet can get hot enough to start a fire.» Why is a duvet dangerous for a charger? | *It traps heat, so the charger can overheat | It makes the charger shiny | It stops electricity from flowing | It is too heavy to lift
